#: ../../source/config_output.rst:3 ../../source/config_output.rst:9
msgid "Output files"
msgstr "输出文件"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:11
msgid ""
"``pc export`` writes 3D and CAD files; ``pc render`` writes 2D projections. "
"Both are configured by a section of ``partcad.yaml`` named after the command "
"-- ``export:`` and ``render:`` -- with one subsection per output file type:"
msgstr ""
"``pc export`` 写出 3D 和 CAD 文件，``pc render`` 写出 2D 投影。两者都由 ``partcad.y"
"aml`` 中以命令命名的小节来配置—— ``export:`` 和 ``render:`` ——其中每种输出文件类型对应一个子小节："

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:37
msgid ""
"The two sections behave identically. Which one a file type belongs to is "
"decided by whichever built-in package implements it (see `Built-in "
"implementations`_) -- ``step`` is an ``export:`` type wherever it is written "
"down, ``svg`` is a ``render:`` one. For a file type no built-in package "
"implements, the section it is declared in is what decides: declare a type of "
"your own under ``export:`` and it is an export type, under ``render:`` and "
"it is a render type."
msgstr ""
"这两个小节的行为完全相同。一个文件类型属于哪一个，取决于实现它的那个内置包（见 `Built-in implementations`_）"
"—— ``step`` 无论写在哪里都是 ``export:`` 类型，而 ``svg`` 是 ``render:`` 类型。对于没有任"
"何内置包实现的文件类型，由它被声明在哪个小节来决定：把自己的类型声明在 ``export:`` 下，它就是导出类型；声明在 ``rend"
"er:`` 下，它就是渲染类型。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:45
msgid ""
"Whichever section owns a file type, the other one is read first and acts as "
"a fallback, so the owning section always wins where both set the same field."
msgstr "无论一个文件类型归哪个小节所有，另一个小节都会被先读取并充当回退，因此在两者设置了同一字段的地方，始终是所属的那个小节胜出。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:48
msgid ""
"For an ``export:`` type the fallback is history: a package that configured "
"its STEP or STL output under ``render:`` before ``export:`` existed keeps "
"working."
msgstr ""
"对 ``export:`` 类型而言，这种回退是历史遗留：在 ``export:`` 出现之前就把 STEP 或 STL 输出配置在 `"
"`render:`` 下的包仍然可以正常工作。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:51
msgid ""
"For a ``render:`` type the fallback is what an export implementation *is*. "
"An export file is one a CAD tool can open as a part or a sketch, which is a "
"stricter thing to be than an output file in general -- so it also serves "
"wherever any output file would do, and a render request for a file type only "
"``export:`` implements uses that implementation."
msgstr ""
"对 ``render:`` 类型而言，这种回退源于导出实现 *本身的性质*。导出文件是 CAD 工具能够作为零件或草图打开的文件，这比一"
"般意义上的输出文件要求更严格——因此它在任何需要输出文件的场合同样适用，而针对只有 ``export:`` 才实现的文件类型发出的渲染请"
"求，就会使用那个实现。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:57
msgid ""
"Note that neither fallback has anything to do with which command was typed. "
"``pc export`` and ``pc render`` differ in their defaults, not in the section "
"they read: a file type declared only under ``render:`` is produced by ``pc "
"export -t <type>`` just as well, because the section follows the declaration "
"and not the command."
msgstr ""
"注意，这两种回退都与键入的是哪条命令无关。两条命令 ``pc export`` 和 ``pc render`` 的差别在于默认值，而不在"
"于读取哪个小节：只声明在 ``render:`` 下的文件类型，用 ``pc export -t <type>`` 同样可以产生，因为小"
"节跟随的是声明而不是命令。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:63
msgid ""
"What the two sections do say is what a file type *is*, and that is worth "
"getting right when publishing a package. Declare a type under ``export:`` "
"and you are promising geometry another tool can go on working with; declare "
"it under ``render:`` and you are promising an output file, nothing more. A "
"drawing, a picture or a report is the latter -- so declare it under ``render:"
"``, where it stays reachable from both commands, rather than under ``export:"
"``, where it would promise a part it cannot deliver."
msgstr ""
"这两个小节真正表明的，是一个文件类型 *是什么*，发布包时这一点值得弄对。把类型声明在 ``export:`` 下，就是在承诺提供另一个"
"工具可以继续处理的几何；声明在 ``render:`` 下，就只是在承诺一个输出文件，仅此而已。工程图、图片或报告属于后者——因此应把它"
"声明在 ``render:`` 下，这样两条命令都仍然能够到达它，而不要声明在 ``export:`` 下，那会承诺一个它无法交付的零件。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:71
msgid ""
"The short form ``<file type>: <path>`` is the same as ``prefix: <path>``."
msgstr "简写形式 ``<file type>: <path>`` 等同于 ``prefix: <path>``。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:74
msgid "Where the file goes"
msgstr "文件写到哪里"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:76
msgid ""
"``prefix`` is the directory the file goes in, relative to the output "
"directory (``-O``) or, failing that, to the package. A ``prefix`` that "
"carries an extension names the file itself, which is the one way to give an "
"object's output a name of its own. Otherwise the file is named after the "
"object, with the extension the file type declares."
msgstr ""
"``prefix`` 是文件所在的目录，相对于输出目录（``-O``）；没有输出目录时则相对于包。带扩展名的 ``prefix`` 指定"
"的是文件本身，这是为某个对象的输出单独命名的唯一方式。否则文件以对象命名，并使用该文件类型声明的扩展名。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:82
msgid ""
"An object whose name carries a ``/`` is written into a sub-directory of that "
"name, and the directories are created on the way. A package may declare an "
"object that way itself, and the objects another file materializes are named "
"that way whether it did or not -- a STEP assembly's components are the parts "
"``<assembly>/<component>``, a URDF's links ``<assembly>/<link>``:"
msgstr ""
"名称中带 ``/`` 的对象会写入同名的子目录，这些目录会在写入过程中一并创建。包可以自己这样声明对象；而由另一个文件实体化出来的对象，"
"无论包是否这样声明，都会这样命名——STEP 装配体的组件就是零件 ``<assembly>/<component>``，URDF 的连"
"杆就是 ``<assembly>/<link>``："

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:93
msgid ""
"The separator in a *name* is always ``/``, whichever operating system reads "
"it, so the same command produces the same tree on Linux, macOS and Windows."
msgstr ""
"*名称* 中的分隔符始终是 ``/``，无论由哪个操作系统读取，因此同一条命令在 Linux、macOS 和 Windows 上产生相同的目录树。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:96
msgid ""
"Every directory an output file needs is created on the way to writing it: "
"the sub-directories a name with a ``/`` in it asks for, and the directory "
"around them that ``-O``, ``prefix`` or ``output_dir`` named and nobody has "
"made. There is nothing to ask for -- the ``-p``/``--create-dirs`` flag that "
"used to draw a line between those two halves of one path is gone, and both "
"halves are made."
msgstr ""
"输出文件需要的每一个目录都会在写入过程中创建：既包括名称中的 ``/`` 所要求的子目录，也包括由 ``-O``、 ``prefix``"
" 或 ``output_dir`` 指定而尚无人创建的外层目录。无需额外提出要求——曾经在同一路径的这两部分之间划出界线的 ``-p``"
" / ``--create-dirs`` 标志已经取消，两部分都会被创建。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:103
msgid "Export parameters"
msgstr "导出参数"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:105
msgid ""
"Every field that is not one of those listed above is a parameter of that "
"file type, handed to whatever implements it. Which parameters exist is "
"therefore up to the implementation, not to PartCAD. For example, the built-"
"in STEP implementation accepts ``comment``, which it places into the STEP "
"file's ``FILE_DESCRIPTION`` header entity:"
msgstr ""
"凡是不在上面所列之内的字段，都是该文件类型的参数，会被交给它的实现。因此存在哪些参数取决于实现，而不取决于 PartCAD。例如内置的 "
"STEP 实现接受 ``comment``，并把它放进 STEP 文件的 ``FILE_DESCRIPTION`` 头实体中："

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:117
msgid ""
"Every STEP file the package produces -- for any part or assembly in it -- "
"then carries that text."
msgstr "此后该包产生的每一个 STEP 文件——无论对应其中的哪个零件或装配体——都会带上这段文字。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:120
msgid ""
"Parameters may be declared per package, as above, or per object, in which "
"case the object's value wins:"
msgstr "参数可以像上面那样按包声明，也可以按对象声明；按对象声明时以对象的取值为准："

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:132
msgid ""
"A parameter can also be given for one command instead of written down. The "
"two that aim a 2D projection -- ``viewport_origin``, which is where the "
"shape is looked at from, and ``viewport_up``, which way is up in the picture "
"-- are ``pc render --viewport-origin``/``--viewport-up``, with ``--view`` "
"naming the common directions (see :doc:`cli`). Passed that way they layer on "
"top of everything below, package and object alike, for that run only."
msgstr ""
"参数也可以只为一条命令给出，而不写进配置。用于确定 2D 投影方向的那两个参数—— ``viewport_origin`` 表示从什么位"
"置观察形状， ``viewport_up`` 表示图中哪个方向朝上——对应 ``pc render --viewport-origin`"
"` / ``--viewport-up``，而 ``--view`` 为常用的几个方向命名（见 :doc:`cli`）。以这种方式传入时"
"，它们叠加在下面的一切之上，包和对象都一样，并且只对本次运行有效。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:139
msgid "Three names are not entirely the package's own."
msgstr "有三个名字并不完全属于包自己。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:141
msgid ""
"``decode`` is not a parameter at all. It is one of the fields PartCAD reads "
"itself -- it says whether the sandbox rebuilds the shape and assembly "
"envelopes into live geometry before the implementation sees them (see "
"``urdf`` under `Built-in implementations`_) -- so no package can declare an "
"export parameter named ``decode``: a ``decode:`` in a file type's "
"configuration is always that flag."
msgstr ""
"``decode`` 根本不是参数。它是 PartCAD 自己读取的字段之一——它表示沙箱是否在实现看到形状封套和装配体封套之前，把它们"
"重建为可用的几何（见 `Built-in implementations`_ 中的 ``urdf``）——因此没有任何包可以声明名为 `"
"`decode`` 的导出参数：文件类型配置中的 ``decode:`` 永远是那个标志。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:148
msgid ""
"``properties`` is the other way round, and it is a parameter -- with a "
"caveat. A file type that declares ``properties: true`` is handed, in place "
"of the flag, an index of what the shapes being written declare about "
"themselves: their ``physics``, ``material`` and ``color``, keyed by the full "
"``<package>:<name>`` of each shape, so an implementation given a whole "
"assembly tree can look up the properties belonging to each node of it. Only "
"shapes that declare at least one appear."
msgstr ""
"``properties`` 则正好相反，它是一个参数——但有一点需要注意。声明了 ``properties: true`` 的文件类型"
"，收到的不是这个标志本身，而是一份索引，记录被写出的那些形状对自身的声明：它们的 ``physics``、 ``material`` 和"
" ``color``，以每个形状完整的 ``<package>:<name>`` 为键，这样拿到整棵装配树的实现就能查到属于其中每个节点"
"的属性。只有至少声明了其中一项的形状才会出现。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:162
msgid ""
"It is opt-in because building the index instantiates the whole assembly "
"tree, which defeats the shape cache for that subtree: an assembly whose "
"geometry could have been served from the cache has to be built anyway, so "
"that its children exist to be walked. An implementation with no use for the "
"properties should not pay for that. ``urdf`` is the one built-in file type "
"that asks."
msgstr ""
"它需要显式开启，因为构建这份索引会实例化整棵装配树，从而令该子树的形状缓存失效：本可以直接从缓存中取得几何的装配体，仍然必须被构建一遍，"
"好让它的子节点存在以供遍历。用不到这些属性的实现不应该为此付出代价。在内置文件类型中，只有 ``urdf`` 会提出这个要求。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:168
msgid ""
"The caveat is that ``properties``, unlike ``decode``, is *not* a reserved "
"field name, and PartCAD intercepts it by value rather than by declaration: a "
"package that declares an ordinary export parameter of its own named "
"``properties`` and gives it the value ``true`` will find that value replaced "
"by the index before its implementation sees it. Any other value is passed "
"through untouched, but the name is best avoided for anything else."
msgstr ""
"需要注意的是，与 ``decode`` 不同， ``properties`` *不是* 保留字段名，PartCAD 是按取值而不是按声明"
"来拦截它的：如果某个包自己声明了一个名为 ``properties`` 的普通导出参数，并把它的值设为 ``true``，那么在它的实现"
"看到之前，这个值就会被索引替换掉。其他任何取值都会原样传递，但最好不要把这个名字用作别的用途。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:177
msgid ""
"``reproducible`` is the third, and it is a field of the protocol rather than "
"any one format's parameter. It is a boolean, it defaults to ``false``, and "
"it says whether this file has to come out **byte-for-byte the same every "
"time it is written**, from the same object:"
msgstr ""
"``reproducible`` 是第三个，它是协议的字段，而不是某一种格式的参数。它是布尔值，默认为 ``false``，表示由同一个"
"对象写出这个文件时，是否必须 **每一次都得到逐字节相同的结果**："

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:188
msgid ""
"Unlike every other parameter, it is handed to the implementation whether or "
"not anybody declared it -- so an implementation reads "
"``request[\"reproducible\"]`` without first checking that the key is there, "
"and means by it what every other implementation means. That is the whole "
"point of it being here rather than in each format's own list of options: a "
"package that publishes a ``render:`` implementation of its own writes "
"``reproducible`` and it already means this."
msgstr ""
"与其他所有参数不同，无论有没有人声明它，它都会被交给实现——因此实现可以直接读取 ``request[\"reproducible\"]``"
" 而不必先检查这个键是否存在，而且它的含义与其他所有实现中的含义一致。这正是把它放在这里、而不是放进各个格式自己的选项列表里的意义所在："
"发布自有 ``render:`` 实现的包只要写下 ``reproducible``，它就已经是这个含义。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:195
msgid ""
"What it does depends on the file type, and on four of them it does something "
"today:"
msgstr "它具体起什么作用取决于文件类型；目前有四种文件类型会因它而有所不同："

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:198
msgid "``svg``, ``png``, ``jpeg``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:199
msgid ""
"The projection goes through OpenCASCADE's **exact** hidden-line algorithm "
"rather than the polygonal one. The exact algorithm works from the surfaces; "
"the polygonal one works from a triangulation, which is floating point all "
"the way down, so the same shape meshed to the same deflection comes out with "
"a slightly different silhouette on a different architecture."
msgstr ""
"投影改走 OpenCASCADE 的 **精确** 消隐线算法，而不是多边形算法。精确算法基于曲面进行计算；多边形算法基于三角网格进行计"
"算，而三角网格自始至终都是浮点运算，因此同一个形状按相同的偏差网格化之后，在不同体系结构上会得到略有差异的轮廓。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:205
msgid ""
"Every number written into the drawing is also rounded to the ``precision`` "
"the file type claims (ten decimal places by default), and a negative zero is "
"written as zero. Below that precision what is in the file is the last bit of "
"an arithmetic rather than a measurement -- a stroke width that differs in "
"its sixteenth digit, an arc rotated by half a femtodegree -- and it is a "
"diff every time the drawing is produced somewhere new."
msgstr ""
"写入工程图的每一个数字还会按该文件类型声明的 ``precision`` 取整（默认十位小数），负零写作零。在这个精度以下，文件里的内容"
"是算术运算的最后一位，而不是测量的结果——第十六位数字才不同的线宽、旋转了半飞度的圆弧——而每当这张工程图在新的地方产生时，它们都会变成一处差异。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:212
msgid ""
"For ``png`` and ``jpeg`` that settles the picture and not the encoding -- "
"the bytes below the projection are svglib's, reportlab's and Pillow's."
msgstr ""
"对 ``png`` 和 ``jpeg`` 来说，这确定的是画面而不是编码——投影之下的字节来自 svglib、reportlab 和 Pillow。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:215
msgid "``dxf``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:216
msgid ""
"The same, plus fixed header metadata: a DXF is otherwise stamped on every "
"save with the time it was written and a fresh pair of GUIDs, and ezdxf "
"derives the order of its ``CLASSES`` section from a ``set``, so it emits "
"differently per process."
msgstr ""
"同上，另外还会固定头部元数据：否则 DXF 每次保存都会被打上写入时的时间戳和一对新的 GUID，而且 ezdxf 的 ``CLASSE"
"S`` 小节顺序来自一个 ``set``，因而每个进程写出的内容都不一样。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:221
msgid ""
"It is off by default because it is not free. The exact projection is the "
"slower of the two by a wide margin on anything large, and it is the one that "
"can take the sandbox down: every released OpenCASCADE reads past the end of "
"an allocation in the rejection table that algorithm sorts its edge crossings "
"in (`Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1546 <https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/"
"issues/1546>`_), which is a coin flip on an assembly with enough edges. A "
"picture produced to be looked at should be the fastest correct one; a "
"drawing that is *kept*, so that a diff answers whether it changed, is the "
"case that says so. Every image under ``examples/`` in the PartCAD repository "
"sets it."
msgstr ""
"它默认关闭，因为它并非没有代价。在任何较大的模型上，精确投影都要慢得多，而且正是它可能让沙箱崩溃：所有已发布的 OpenCASCADE "
"在该算法用来排序边交点的剔除表中都会越界读取（`Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1546 <https://github.c"
"om/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/issues/1546>`_），在边足够多的装配体上这就是一次抛硬币。为观看而产生的图"
"片，应当是最快得到的那个正确结果；而 *被保留下来*、靠差异来回答它是否发生变化的工程图，才是需要开启它的场合。PartCAD 仓库中 "
"``examples/`` 下的每一张图片都设置了它。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:232
msgid ""
"The rest of the built-in file types accept it and write the same bytes "
"either way. They declare it all the same, so that an implementation which "
"starts reading it does not also have to start receiving it."
msgstr ""
"其余内置文件类型接受这个字段，但无论取值如何都写出相同的字节。它们仍然一律声明它，这样当某个实现开始读取它时，就不必同时还要解决如何收到它的问题。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:236
msgid ""
"What it is not is a promise that two machines produce one file. It removes "
"everything PartCAD chooses -- which algorithm, how a number is written, the "
"clock, the GUIDs, the iteration order of a ``set`` -- and what is left is "
"the CAD kernel's own arithmetic. Two platforms that disagree about a "
"transcendental function in the last bit can still find one intersection more "
"than each other along a curved silhouette, and no amount of rounding makes "
"those two drawings the same file. So two renders on one machine are the same "
"file, and two machines agree on everything but the hardest subjects. That is "
"why PartCAD's own ``Examples (PartCAD)`` job compares the checked-in "
"drawings on one cell of its matrix rather than on all of them."
msgstr ""
"它并不是在承诺两台机器会产生同一个文件。它消除的是一切由 PartCAD 决定的东西——用哪种算法、数字如何书写、时钟、GUID、``s"
"et`` 的迭代顺序——剩下的则是 CAD 内核自己的算术。两个平台若对某个超越函数的最后一位有分歧，沿着弯曲的轮廓仍然可能比对方多找出"
"一个交点，再怎么取整也无法让这两张工程图成为同一个文件。因此，同一台机器上的两次渲染会得到同一个文件，而两台机器则在除最棘手的对象之外的"
"一切上保持一致。这就是为什么 PartCAD 自己的 ``Examples (PartCAD)`` 作业只在矩阵的一个单元上比对签入的工"
"程图，而不是在所有单元上比对。"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:248
msgid "Custom implementations"
msgstr "自定义实现"

#: ../../source/config_output.rst:250
msgid ""
"Declaring ``path`` for a file type replaces the implementation itself with a "
"script the package supplies. This is the same mechanism as a ``partType`` "
"wrapper: the script runs inside a PartCAD sandbox, so it may import OCP, "
"build123d or CadQuery, and it is executed with two globals available --"
